WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.161
What is a mural?.

2
00:00:01.321 --> 00:00:03.457
A mural is a picture painted on a wall.

3
00:00:03.617 --> 00:00:10.583
It is for everyone who walks past, and it usually has a job: to welcome, to cheer, or to ask people to do something.

4
00:00:11.283 --> 00:00:12.444
Plan it small.

5
00:00:12.604 --> 00:00:14.555
A mural is too big to get wrong.

6
00:00:14.715 --> 00:00:21.356
So decide the message, think about who will see it, sketch ideas, and make a small mock-up.

7
00:00:21.516 --> 00:00:23.327
Then ask people what they think.

8
00:00:24.027 --> 00:00:25.420
Think about the audience.

9
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.273
The audience is the people who will see your mural.

10
00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:31.684
Small children need big pictures, not long words.

11
00:00:31.844 --> 00:00:34.027
A dark corridor needs bright colours.

12
00:00:34.187 --> 00:00:35.812
Change your design for them.

13
00:00:36.512 --> 00:00:37.859
Painted houses.

14
00:00:38.019 --> 00:00:43.592
In South Africa, Ndebele women paint their homes with bold shapes and thick black outlines.

15
00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:48.628
The designs are passed down from mothers to daughters, and they make each home stand out.
